※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4364

※ **A function taking a list as its own is no value of the system's
※ convention.**  A call by name sees to it that the room it changes in place is
※ room nobody else holds, copying where it has to; a call of an address is the
※ code at the address and nothing else, so nothing would make the copy.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[cdecl]
fn pushed(l: mut [u8], x: u8) → [u8]:
    l ⧺← [x]
    l

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let f: @[cdecl] fn([u8], u8) → [u8] = pushed
    if #f([], 1u8) = 1: 0u6 else: 1u6
